  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved food and livelihood security in Bangladesh (Dhaka Ahsania Mission)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is part of a programme in which four Bangladeshi partners are collaborating together in order to address food and livelihood insecurity, which were identified as the key problems in Bagerhat district.  The partners hold regular meetings and build up linkages with other networks through which monitoring information, reviews, evaluations and experiences can be shared.  Dhaka Ahsania Mission (DAM) is taking a lead role in training community disaster preparedness, focusing on education;  and production of materials for training of communities through community action groups, and strengthening disaster management committees at union and upazila levels (ie at the two lowest local government levels); and liaison with local government at district level.  DAM is also engaged promoting tree and homestead plantations, and developing advocacy and publication materials.</narrative>
  </description>
